e_span and its source basis. Unknown cessation does not establish publication to the present."}],"continuation":{"status":"unknown","basis":"The existing catalogue does not establish present-day publication continuity."},"interpretation":"Explicit selection from the existing entry and bibliography. Original source reading limits remain; no new whole-work verification or field survey is claimed.","prepared_on":"2026-10-15","editorial_record":"data/production-batches/chronology-1.141/acceptance.json","unresolved":["Retain exact title/edition, source and holdings distinctions; no unrecorded cessation or current-status claim."]}}],"edges":[{"id":"journal_venue_jsh_social_foundation","target":"social","relationship_kind":"founded_for","relationship":"Founded in 1967 as an institutional home for the emerging social-history programme Peter Stearns sought to establish within the discipline.","basis":"sourced_founding_programme","temporal_scope":{"start":1967,"end":1967,"precision":"year","meaning":"founding_event"},"source_ids":["journal_source_jsh_mission"],"evidence_note":"Censer’s publisher abstract explicitly connects the founding with Stearns’s effort to establish the field’s disciplinary position. This does not date the origin of all social history or assert that the journal founded the entire field.","source":"journal_0ade3b13475fde7c","directed":true,"checked_on":"2026-09-13"},{"id":"journal_venue_hwj_workshop_foundation","target":"historyworkshop","relationship_kind":"founded_for","relationship":"Founded in 1976 by History Workshop activists to advance collaborative, democratic historical work through a journal of socialist historians.","basis":"sourced_founding_programme","temporal_scope":{"start":1976,"end":1976,"precision":"year","meaning":"founding_event"},"source_ids":["journal_source_hwj_history"],"evidence_note":"The movement’s institutional account links the 1976 journal to its democratic-history purpose and 1975 manifesto. Feminist commitments developed further; the later subtitle is not projected unchanged onto 1976.","source":"journal_84203dbdbd3796c3","directed":true,"checked_on":"2026-09-13"},{"id":"journal_venue_annales_founding_programme","target":"annales","relationship_kind":"founded_for","relationship":"Launched in 1929 to develop economic and social history across the divisions separating historians and researchers of contemporary societies.","basis":"primary_founding_editorial","temporal_scope":{"start":1929,"end":1929,"precision":"year","meaning":"founding_event"},"source_ids":["journal_source_annales_manifesto"],"evidence_note":"Bloch and Febvre’s first editorial states the interdisciplinary problem motivating the new periodical. The target is the atlas entry that includes this founding project, not a claim that every later Annales approach already existed. This record names the 1929 title rather than assigning its founding date to an unverified modern-title run.","source":"journal_dc31870ec1f950f5","directed":true,"checked_on":"2026-09-13"},{"id":"journal_venue_past_present_narrative_debate","target":"revival","relationship_kind":"site_of_debate","relationship":"Hosted Stone’s 1979 Revival of Narrative essay and Hobsbawm’s 1980 comments, providing a concrete entry into the narrative-versus-structural-explanation controversy.","basis":"named_published_exchange","debate_name":"Revival of narrative: Stone–Hobsbawm exchange","temporal_scope":{"start":1979,"end":1980,"precision":"year","meaning":"documented_exchange"},"source_ids":["journal_source_stone_narrative","journal_source_hobsbawm_narrative"],"evidence_note":"Two publisher records identify the opening essay and named follow-up in adjacent issues. The existing revival entry supplies the qualified debate context. The journal hosted the disagreement; it did not endorse one side, and this exchange did not terminate quantitative history.","source":"journal_b2aca6e2c5b0a211","directed":true,"checked_on":"2026-09-13"},{"id":"journal_venue_past_present_founding_programme","source":"journal_b2aca6e2c5b0a211","target":"marx","relationship_kind":"founded_for","directed":true,"relationship":"Founded in 1952 through a coalition involving British Marxist historians to advance historical research for readers across periods, regions and specialisms.","basis":"sourced_founding_programme","temporal_scope":{"start":1952,"end":1952,"precision":"year","meaning":"founding_event"},"source_ids":["journal_source_pp_editors_250","journal_source_pp_ihr_marxist_history"],"evidence_note":"The link locates a journal-building initiative within Marxist social history while retaining its generalist purpose and participation beyond Marxism. It does not identify the journal as exclusively Marxist, date the birth of social history to 1952, or replace its separate narrative-debate edge.","checked_on":"2026-09-15"},{"id":"journal_venue_technology_culture_founding_programme","source":"journal_38e479e715d9523d","target":"technology","relationship_kind":"founded_for","directed":true,"relationship":"Launched in 1959 following the joint planning of SHOT and its journal, with a programme of bringing disciplines together in the history of technology.","basis":"sourced_founding_programme","temporal_scope":{"start":1959,"end":1959,"precision":"year","meaning":"founding_event"},"source_ids":["journal_source_technology_kranzberg_memorial"],"evidence_note":"Participant recollections connect the 1958 institutional decision to the first-issue programme. The edge records institutional consolidation and interdisciplinary intent; older histories of technology are not erased and subsequent practice is not inferred from the manifesto.","checked_on":"2026-09-15"},{"id":"journal_venue_gg_founding_programme","source":"journal_a67e93621de863b1","target":"bielefeld","relationship_kind":"founded_for","directed":true,"relationship":"Launched in 1975 with a programme connecting historical inquiry and social-scientific analysis through thematic issues, research reports and discussion.","basis":"primary_founding_editorial","temporal_scope":{"start":1975,"end":1975,"precision":"year","meaning":"founding_event"},"source_ids":["journal_source_gg_founders_preface"],"evidence_note":"Uses the already reviewed four-author founding foreword. Historical social science is broader than Sonderweg; neither all later journal contents nor every contributor is assigned to a single doctrine. The announced editorial mechanisms are not an audit of implementation.","checked_on":"2026-09-15"},{"id":"journal_venue_negro_history_founding_programme","source":"journal_1c7b5476f23090dc","target":"black","relationship_kind":"founded_for","directed":true,"relationship":"Launched in 1916 under Carter G. Woodson and ASNLH to preserve, publish and expand knowledge of Black historical experience and contributions.","basis":"sourced_founding_programme","temporal_scope":{"start":1916,"end":1916,"precision":"year","meaning":"founding_event"},"source_ids":["journal_source_jnh_first_volume_reception"],"evidence_note":"Contemporary reception reproduced in volume 1 describes the recovery and documentation programme. This institutional milestone falls within the atlas’s earlier roots; Black historical thought predates the journal. The 1916 original title remains distinct from the 2002 Journal of African American History title.","checked_on":"2026-09-15"},{"id":"journal_venue_isis_founding_programme","source":"journal_8ca2dcb0199b28f9","target":"science","relationship_kind":"founded_for","directed":true,"relationship":"Established as a project in 1912 to institutionalize history of science through Sarton’s programme of historical synthesis, set out in the first volume published in 1913.","basis":"sourced_founding_programme","temporal_scope":{"start":1912,"end":1912,"precision":"year","meaning":"founding_event"},"source_ids":["journal_source_isis_foundation"],"evidence_note":"Preserves the existing 1912 foundation date and explicitly distinguishes 1913 first publication. The initial Sartonian synthesis is one programme within history of science; it does not characterize the entire field or the journal’s later pluralism.","checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_environmental_review_field_formation","source":"journal_919d0c14e01dd6ed","target":"environment","relationship_kind":"founded_for","directed":true,"relationship":"Launched in 1976 as part of the organizing effort that established an institutional community for environmental history in the United States and produced ASEH in 1977.","basis":"sourced_founding_programme","temporal_scope":{"start":1976,"end":1976,"precision":"year","meaning":"founding_event"},"source_ids":["journal_source_aseh_founding_history","journal_source_oup_environmental_merger"],"evidence_note":"The journal and society were planned together to organize an emerging field. This institutional formation is distinct from the later 1990 renaming, 1996 merger and the separate Environment and History launched in 1995. It does not make US institutionalization the origin of all environmental historical thought.","checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_signs_women_principal","source":"journal_8764d21a3f246bf9","target":"women","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained interdisciplinary venue for women’s history.","evidence_note":"Norberg reviews historical writing across the journal’s first decades, including suffrage research; Smith-Rosenberg’s 1975 essay is an early anchor.","selection_note":"Selected for sustained historical contributions within feminist scholarship. This is a women’s-history link, not a claim that every article is historical or that the journal founded the field.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_signs40"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1975,"end":1999,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. The endpoint limits this review, not the journal’s later importance."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_feminist_studies_women_principal","source":"journal_1bf8df84e3283ad5","target":"women","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing feminist forum publishing women’s history and historical special issues.","evidence_note":"Institutional history documents connections with historians; Norberg identifies an enduring historical publishing role.","selection_note":"Selected for a sustained historical strand in an interdisciplinary journal, rather than an exclusive disciplinary identity.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_feminist_studies","journal_source_venue_review_signs40"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1972,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_gender_history_gender_principal","source":"journal_a00c9347fa743603","target":"gender","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A specialist venue for feminist gender history during the 1990s.","evidence_note":"Norberg’s retrospective identifies the journal as a dedicated feminist-history outlet from 1989; the earlier institutional-history source supports its launch context.","selection_note":"Selected for the gender-history part of the atlas entry. This does not establish equivalent coverage of every racial-formation approach in that broad entry.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_signs40","journal_source_gender_history_foundation"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1989,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_women_history_women_principal","source":"journal_ec74f244f54d7364","target":"women","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A specialist venue connecting women’s history with feminist and gender analysis.","evidence_note":"Meade and Rupp trace a continuing forum from its diverse first volume through later methodological debates.","selection_note":"Selected for dedicated historical publishing. The retrospective rejects a simple progression from an exclusively white, US-centred beginning; this selection retains that qualification.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_women25"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1989,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_cssh_historical_sociology_principal","source":"journal_647183c1e131cf7a","target":"historicalsociology","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing interdisciplinary venue for comparative historical analysis.","evidence_note":"The anniversary foreword describes an enduring comparative forum. Wallerstein (1974) and Scott/Tilly (1975) provide dated examples.","selection_note":"Selected as a bridge between history and social analysis, with a remit broader than the entry’s state/class comparisons; not an exclusive organ of historical sociology.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_cssh50","journal_source_venue_review_atlas_wallerstein_rise_primary","journal_source_venue_review_atlas_scott_tilly_work"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1958,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_cssh_anthropology_principal","source":"journal_647183c1e131cf7a","target":"anthropology","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A venue for sustained exchanges between anthropological theory and historical inquiry.","evidence_note":"Ortner’s 1984 theoretical review and Medick’s 1987 methodological intervention anchor this bounded selection within the journal’s comparative editorial tradition.","selection_note":"Selected for the history–anthropology interface, not for all anthropology. The short interval follows the reviewed contributions; wider coverage needs further review.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_cssh50","journal_source_venue_review_atlas_ortner_practice_primary","journal_source_venue_review_atlas_medick_missionaries"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1984,"end":1987,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. The endpoint limits this review, not the journal’s later importance."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_ssh_social_principal","source":"journal_03730bc252490e14","target":"social","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained institutional venue for historical social-science research.","evidence_note":"McCants traces continuity of the association journal’s analytical mission across forty years.","selection_note":"Selected for the social-science strand within new social history. It does not stand for all forms of social history.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_ssh40"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1976,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_ssh_quant_principal","source":"journal_03730bc252490e14","target":"quant","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing venue for quantitative work within historical social science.","evidence_note":"The retrospective explicitly locates quantitative alongside qualitative methods in the journal’s continuing programme.","selection_note":"Selected as an interdisciplinary home for quantitative approaches, without making quantification its sole method or the source of the entire field.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_ssh40"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1976,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_ehr_economic_principal","source":"journal_aa1243d525819115","target":"economic","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained society journal for economic and social history.","evidence_note":"The centenary study follows the Review across several periods rather than relying only on its founding mission.","selection_note":"Selected for an enduring disciplinary role; economic history has much earlier intellectual roots.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_ehr100"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1927,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_ehr_social_principal","source":"journal_aa1243d525819115","target":"social","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing venue for social history intertwined with economic inquiry.","evidence_note":"The sampled contents document recurring labour, demographic and social-structure research, with changing methods.","selection_note":"Selected for the economic/social intersection. Its technical turn does not represent the whole new-social-history movement.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_ehr100"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1960,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_ohr_oral_principal","source":"journal_b37c47d6d6bf8912","target":"oral","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing forum for oral-history method, interpretation and practice.","evidence_note":"The retrospective identifies contributions by Haley (1973), Grele (1978), Frisch (1979), feminist methodologists (1987), Portelli (1992) and Yow (1997).","selection_note":"Selected for a sustained methodological conversation. The source’s US emphasis limits global representativeness; later articles do not extend this reviewed interval.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_ohr50"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1973,"end":1997,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. The endpoint limits this review, not the journal’s later importance."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_jih_quant_principal","source":"journal_186238c00e627d8e","target":"quant","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained venue for quantitative approaches to historical questions.","evidence_note":"The editors identify quantification as a continuing contribution across the journal’s five decades.","selection_note":"Selected for methodological continuity within a broader interdisciplinary programme; neither all interdisciplinary history nor all its articles are quantitative.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_jih50"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1970,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_jih_demography_principal","source":"journal_186238c00e627d8e","target":"demography","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"An interdisciplinary venue for historical population research.","evidence_note":"The retrospective highlights population reconstruction and demographic leadership in its publication history.","selection_note":"Selected for historical-demographic work. This does not establish equal coverage of every approach to family history in the combined atlas entry.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_jih50"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1970,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_isis_science_principal","source":"journal_8ca2dcb0199b28f9","target":"science","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained institutional and intellectual venue for the history of science.","evidence_note":"Holton follows successive generations and changing subject matter through the twentieth century.","selection_note":"Selected for continuity across changing programmes. Later pluralism is not assimilated to Sarton’s original vision, and venue publication begins with the 1913 volume.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_isis100"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1913,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_nations_nationalism_principal","source":"journal_50d38721b9dc530b","target":"nationalismstudies","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A dedicated forum consolidating interdisciplinary nationalism studies.","evidence_note":"Hutchinson describes an existing field gaining a continuing forum, including early theoretical exchanges and a 1996 symposium.","selection_note":"Selected for consolidation and discussion within the atlas’s final decade; not for founding nationalism studies.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_nations25"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1995,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_history_theory_philhist_principal","source":"journal_9c2f011afd81d28b","target":"philhistory","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing specialist forum for the theory and philosophy of history.","evidence_note":"The editor describes successive decades of editorial work and almost annual thematic issues.","selection_note":"Selected for sustained disciplinary discussion, wider than the atlas entry’s explanation/objectivity debates. No single philosophical position is attributed to the journal.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_history_theory"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1960,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_nlr_marx_principal","source":"journal_cf610a9513553000","target":"marx","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing forum for Marxist historical interpretation and debate.","evidence_note":"The retrospective follows historical arguments through successive editorial phases, beginning with the British-development theses.","selection_note":"Selected for historical contributions within a broader political/theoretical review. British New Left Review is not equated with the atlas’s US New Left entry.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_nlr50"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1964,"end":1999,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. The endpoint limits this review, not the journal’s later importance."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_jsh_social_principal","source":"journal_0ade3b13475fde7c","target":"social","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained institutional home for new social history.","evidence_note":"Censer’s retrospective abstract explicitly describes the journal’s continuing field role and accommodation of methodological changes.","selection_note":"Selected on a specific scholarly historical assessment. Full-article details have not been verified; the entry does not claim comprehensive worldwide representation.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_jsh50"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1967,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_hwj_workshop_principal","source":"journal_84203dbdbd3796c3","target":"historyworkshop","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing journal associated with the History Workshop movement and its changing practice.","evidence_note":"The institutional retrospective and contributions in 1976 and 1995 anchor continuity alongside changes of method and audience.","selection_note":"Selected for its direct movement relationship. The journal’s trajectory is not identical to the workshops or to the later digital magazine.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_hwj_history","journal_source_venue_review_atlas_samuel_local_oral","journal_source_venue_review_atlas_massey_places_pasts"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1976,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_past_present_social_principal","source":"journal_b2aca6e2c5b0a211","target":"social","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A generalist journal with a sustained role in social-historical research.","evidence_note":"The retrospective connects labour, social power and cultural interpretation through articles selected across five decades.","selection_note":"Selected for sustained social-historical contributions within a generalist journal. Its authors and methods are broader than one school.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_past250"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1952,"end":1995,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. The endpoint limits this review, not the journal’s later importance."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_past_present_culture_principal","source":"journal_b2aca6e2c5b0a211","target":"culture","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A venue for cultural interpretation within historical research.","evidence_note":"The editors discuss Davis’s 1981 social-symbolic analysis and Stewart’s 1995 imperial-cultural interpretation and its disputed reception.","selection_note":"Selected for a cultural-history strand rather than a separate journal-wide doctrine or founding role.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_past250"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1981,"end":1995,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. The endpoint limits this review, not the journal’s later importance."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_history_africa_method_principal","source":"journal_55b2862e091c93c6","target":"africanhist","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained methodological forum within African history.","evidence_note":"Doortmont’s volume survey identifies a continuing niche in source criticism, archival reporting and methodological debate.","selection_note":"Selected for method within an already established field. The interval starts with the reported first-volume appearance; the journal did not found African history.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_hia38"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1975,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_technology_culture_principal","source":"journal_38e479e715d9523d","target":"technology","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing institutional venue in the development of history of technology.","evidence_note":"Participant accounts connect journal editing with the developing scholarly community through Kranzberg’s editorship.","selection_note":"Selected for a documented institutional role; this interval ends at the reviewed editorial handover, not the end of the journal’s importance.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_shot_memorial"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1959,"end":1981,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. The endpoint limits this review, not the journal’s later importance."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_world_history_global_principal","source":"journal_77695299ceedc9b2","target":"global","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"An institutional forum for world-history research during the 1990s.","evidence_note":"The association’s retrospective explicitly identifies a continuing central role under Bentley, who edited it from 1990.","selection_note":"Selected for world-history community consolidation, not for founding all global or connected history. Evidence is a scoped indexed extract; full tribute remains unread.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_world_history_bentley"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1990,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_environmental_review_environment_principal","source":"journal_919d0c14e01dd6ed","target":"environment","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A principal society venue for environmental-history scholarship during this title interval.","evidence_note":"ASEH’s history identifies the continuing institutional publication role across separately recorded titles.","selection_note":"Selected for the North American society community; the wider international field is not reduced to this lineage.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_aseh_venue_history","journal_source_oup_environmental_merger"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1976,"end":1989,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. The endpoint limits this review, not the journal’s later importance."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_environmental_history_review_environment_principal","source":"journal_57a3505b8688a2ce","target":"environment","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A principal society venue for environmental-history scholarship during this title interval.","evidence_note":"ASEH’s history identifies the continuing institutional publication role across separately recorded titles.","selection_note":"Selected for the North American society community; the wider international field is not reduced to this lineage.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_aseh_venue_history","journal_source_oup_environmental_merger"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1990,"end":1995,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. The endpoint limits this review, not the journal’s later importance."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_environmental_history_environment_principal","source":"journal_b8bc3aaecbd1501f","target":"environment","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A principal society venue for environmental-history scholarship during this title interval.","evidence_note":"ASEH’s history identifies the continuing institutional publication role across separately recorded titles.","selection_note":"Selected for the North American society community; the wider international field is not reduced to this lineage.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_aseh_venue_history","journal_source_oup_environmental_merger"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1996,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Selected evidentiary interval; neither the field’s lifespan nor a publication start/cessation claim. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_shps_bloor_latour_debate","source":"journal_ffdacf6e082def6b","target":"ssk","relationship_kind":"site_of_debate","basis":"named_published_exchange","directed":true,"debate_name":"Bloor–Latour exchange on symmetry and the sociology of scientific knowledge","relationship":"Published Bloor’s Anti-Latour and Latour’s reply in volume 30(1), 1999.","evidence_note":"Previously read primary passages establish an explicit exchange at pp. 81–112 and 113–129. Hosting implies no endorsement. Bloor’s final rejoinder remains unread.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_atlas_bloor_anti_latour_primary","journal_source_venue_review_atlas_latour_bloor_reply_primary"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1999,"end":1999,"precision":"year","meaning":"published_exchange"},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_nations_warwick_debate","source":"journal_50d38721b9dc530b","target":"nationalismstudies","relationship_kind":"site_of_debate","basis":"named_published_exchange","directed":true,"debate_name":"Warwick debate: Anthony D. Smith and Ernest Gellner","relationship":"Published the Smith–Gellner exchange on nations and nationalism in 1996.","evidence_note":"The discussion occurred in 1995; this edge dates publication. Smith’s qualified ethno-symbolic position and Gellner’s modernism remain distinct, without assigning either to the journal.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_review_atlas_warwick_nationalism","journal_source_venue_review_gellner_warwick"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1996,"end":1996,"precision":"year","meaning":"published_exchange"},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_quaderni_micro_principal","source":"journal_cfc410ef907bdbd7","target":"micro","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A collective research forum for Italian microhistory.","evidence_note":"Raggio reconstructs collaborative editorial practice through issues on family/community (1976), villages (1981), local conflict (1986) and land markets (1987).","selection_note":"Selected for the Italian microhistory strand; it does not represent every form of microhistory or German Alltagsgeschichte. The journal predated this programme.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_raggio_microstoria"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1976,"end":1987,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. Later importance is not assessed by this endpoint."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_jhsn_african_principal","source":"journal_ef7022c2c9b569d4","target":"africanhist","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A society forum for the development of African historical scholarship in Nigeria.","evidence_note":"The study follows changing methods and historical contributions across the 1950s, 1960s and 1970s.","selection_note":"Selected for the Nigerian scholarly community and African agency. Nigeria increasingly predominates; the study also identifies limited women’s-history coverage.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_jhsn_review","journal_source_venue_116_jhsn_identity"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1956,"end":1980,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. Later importance is not assessed by this endpoint."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_jhsn_anticolonial_principal","source":"journal_ef7022c2c9b569d4","target":"anticolonial","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained forum for decolonizing accounts of Africa’s past.","evidence_note":"The retrospective traces challenges to colonial narratives and methodological change across the reviewed period.","selection_note":"Selected for a Nigerian anti-colonial historiographical strand, not all liberation theories or all African scholarship. Nationalist interpretation and economic relevance remain contested.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_jhsn_review"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1956,"end":1980,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. Later importance is not assessed by this endpoint."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_ethnohistory_indigenous_principal","source":"journal_e6929b124f9137bc","target":"indigenous","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"An enduring interdisciplinary venue for historical research on Indigenous peoples, especially in the Americas.","evidence_note":"The society history and longitudinal abstract establish continuing publication and changing research scope.","selection_note":"Selected as an ethnohistorical interlocutor within this broad entry. Publication about Indigenous peoples does not establish Indigenous control of research or endorsement of decolonizing methods.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_ethnohistory60","journal_source_venue_116_ethnohistory_society"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1954,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_mouvement_social_principal","source":"journal_054d070a681aafc6","target":"social","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained French venue for labour history and an expanding social history.","evidence_note":"Ceamanos traces four decades of institutionalization and changes in questions, communities and methods.","selection_note":"Selected for the French labour/social-history community. The predecessor L’Actualité de l’Histoire is not backdated under this title; no exclusive Marxist affiliation is inferred.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_mouvement40"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1960,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_negro_history_black_principal","source":"journal_1c7b5476f23090dc","target":"black","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing institutional and scholarly home for African American history.","evidence_note":"Dagbovie traces the journal’s role across successive editorial generations, beyond Woodson’s initial programme.","selection_note":"Selected for sustained African American historical scholarship. The original title applies throughout this interval; the 2002 renaming does not truncate the field’s history.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_jnh_century"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1916,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_annales_original_school_principal","source":"journal_dc31870ec1f950f5","target":"annales","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"The early journal forum associated with the Annales movement.","evidence_note":"Burke’s previously checked generational history supports this early phase; publisher chronology bounds the original title.","selection_note":"Selected for the movement’s early journal community. This supplements the founding edge; it does not imply a uniform doctrine or erase antecedents.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_burke_annales_context","journal_source_venue_116_annales_chronology"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1929,"end":1938,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. Later importance is not assessed by this endpoint."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_annales_esc_school_principal","source":"journal_b5b188191ea8d9f7","target":"annales","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained postwar journal forum for successive Annales approaches.","evidence_note":"The generational history, 1988–1989 editorial reconsideration and Conrad’s transition analysis support the postwar interval.","selection_note":"Selected across changing programmes, not as one unchanging school. The ESC title ends in 1993; the publication continues.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_burke_annales_context","journal_source_venue_116_annales_critical_editorials","journal_source_venue_116_annales_conrad","journal_source_venue_116_annales_chronology"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1946,"end":1993,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. Later importance is not assessed by this endpoint."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_annales_hss_school_principal","source":"journal_65dd21715536a35f","target":"annales","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing Annales forum for historical inquiry in dialogue with the social sciences.","evidence_note":"Conrad studies the 1990s editorial transition and recurring thematic work; publisher chronology identifies the 1994 subtitle change.","selection_note":"Selected for the journal community’s continued, self-critical development. Its refusal of doctrinal closure is retained; this is not an extension of Braudel’s programme unchanged.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_annales_conrad","journal_source_venue_116_annales_chronology"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1994,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_social_studies_science_sts_principal","source":"journal_f8b473560ddb39a0","target":"sts","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"An established interdisciplinary forum for science and technology studies.","evidence_note":"Sismondo’s retrospective identifies an established field role by the late 1970s and editorial continuity through 2002; the 1984 Pinch–Bijker contribution anchors the technology interface.","selection_note":"Selected from 1980, after the documented late-1970s consolidation. Evidence includes a limited indexed retrospective; STS is broader than SSK and no exclusive school allegiance is assigned.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_sss_sismondo","journal_source_venue_116_pinch_bijker","journal_source_venue_116_sss_title"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1980,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_history_sexuality_queer_principal","source":"journal_07ccddae5a67c1fa","target":"queer","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A specialist forum for historical studies of sexuality during the 1990s.","evidence_note":"Nye’s twenty-year retrospective abstract reviews changing questions, periods and methods, particularly women’s sexuality; the opening identifies the 1990 launch.","selection_note":"Selected for sexuality history within the combined sexuality/queer entry, not as a journal uniformly committed to queer theory. Full-text review remains a follow-up.","source_ids":["journal_source_venue_116_nye_sexuality"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1990,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Evidenced selection interval, not a field lifespan or a claim of journal cessation. 2000 is the atlas coverage boundary. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_public_historian_publichistory_principal","source":"journal_d990835e95820881","target":"publichistory","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing professional forum for public history.","evidence_note":"Kelley’s initial programme and NCPH’s institutional account establish its continuing UCSB and society role.","selection_note":"Selected for the US professional community; institutional continuity supports the interval, without a complete article census or global priority claim.","source_ids":["journal_source_gap117_ncph_journal_history_2012","journal_source_gap117_kelley_public_1978"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1978,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Reviewed historical role; 2000 is the atlas boundary. A title-phase endpoint is not the end of the field. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_social_medicine_medicalhistory_principal","source":"journal_6d9388bf4f2e1a99","target":"medicalhistory","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A society forum for social histories of medicine.","evidence_note":"The anniversary review places successive pre-2001 articles within the journal’s continuing programme.","selection_note":"One important social-history venue within a broader field; the 1988 journal launch does not found medical history.","source_ids":["journal_source_gap117_shm_chairs_2020"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1988,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Reviewed historical role; 2000 is the atlas boundary. A title-phase endpoint is not the end of the field. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_urban_yearbook_urbanhistory_principal","source":"journal_68059c6f3fc86951","target":"urbanhistory","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A sustained forum organizing urban historical inquiry.","evidence_note":"The 1974 programme, 1979 appreciation and 1992 retrospective establish the Yearbook’s institutional role.","selection_note":"Title phase of a continuing forum; broader urban historiography predates it.","source_ids":["journal_source_gap117_urban_history_anniversary","journal_source_gap117_urban_titles"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1974,"end":1991,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Reviewed historical role; 2000 is the atlas boundary. A title-phase endpoint is not the end of the field."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"},{"id":"journal_venue_urban_history_urbanhistory_principal","source":"journal_97cc033e49a4f22b","target":"urbanhistory","relationship_kind":"principal_venue","basis":"editorial_longitudinal_review","directed":true,"relationship":"A continuing forum for urban historical research and debate.","evidence_note":"Rodger’s 1992 retrospect, Lees’s 1994 intervention and Lilley’s 2000 study document continuation and variety.","selection_note":"Selected within the wider field; the journal is not identical with one national school.","source_ids":["journal_source_gap117_urban_history_anniversary","journal_source_gap117_urban_titles"],"temporal_scope":{"start":1992,"end":null,"precision":"year","meaning":"reviewed_role_interval","note":"Reviewed historical role; 2000 is the atlas boundary. A title-phase endpoint is not the end of the field. Open from revision 1.133: 2000 was the atlas boundary."},"checked_on":"2026-09-16"}],"sources":[{"id":"journal_source_wikipedia","title":"Wikipedia: List of history journals","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_history_journals","revision_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=List_of_history_journals&oldid=1363535805","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"directory_read","note":"A selective directory, not a census or quality ranking. Categories are directory evidence, not independently checked publisher scopes. Includes historical titles and some magazines/review venues.","attribution":"Wikipedia attribution: CC BY-SA; extracted journal titles and directory classifications. No article prose reproduced.","html_sha256":"3b16b180c420a0a6e9a4bc64521ff444bdc3324890c070ae2cc3d2005f2e26f5"},{"id":"journal_source_sheet_271","title":"User-supplied spreadsheet: 271 title rows","url":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Gp-wHW0Sxqas38YteBk3uennT-kjpP32XOjf_wC8WZs/edit?gid=0","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"csv_read","note":"Titles only. Original compiler, selection rules and reuse license not established; no PJIP affiliation assumed.","input_file":"raw/user-sheet-271.csv","sha256":"4d088b188eeddbb13e973559d7fd09ba7187402aeebcd482d2f5bbf664313e5f"},{"id":"journal_source_sheet_1389","title":"User-supplied spreadsheet: 1,389 title rows","url":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1-d7jkVFvQ-OUqyrOJgow7-ocCzpU26QRAre3ciw8a3Q/edit?gid=641273133","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"csv_read","note":"Titles only, including a repeated title. No country, language, ISSN, publisher or scope columns; no PJIP affiliation assumed.","input_file":"raw/user-sheet-1389.csv","sha256":"1279028bce12e5bfb86e4028b996452e9f2e9cd9223b3fd37a6172855c6a4899"},{"id":"journal_source_ooir","title":"User transcription attributed to OOIR: approximate Impact Factor 2025","url":"https://ooir.org/journals.php?field=History+%26+Archaeology&category=History&metric=jif","checked_on":null,"verification":"user_transcription","note":"Source page returned HTTP 403. Values retain the user’s approximate 2025 label; they are not independently verified JCR figures or quality tiers.","input_file":"raw/ooir-user-transcription.tsv","sha256":"1d22506faa31c8e4b227ee3ee83c420dc8ec331a2e8f7d791cabb8e467c39234"},{"id":"journal_source_oup_jsh","title":"Journal of Social History: publisher remit","url":"https://academic.oup.com/jsh","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"publisher_scope_read","note":"Publisher describes social-history research across regions, from the early modern period onward. Link concerns subject coverage, not adherence to every programme in the New social history atlas entry."},{"id":"journal_source_wiley_gender","title":"Gender & History: publisher remit","url":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/journal/14680424","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"publisher_scope_read","note":"Publisher remit covers femininity, masculinity and gender relations across historical contexts. Venue links concern these subjects, not every argument or strand in the atlas entries."},{"id":"journal_source_tf_oral","title":"Oral History Review: publisher remit","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/journals/uohr20","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"publisher_scope_read","note":"Publisher remit explicitly covers oral-history theory and practice. Founding date and ISSNs not checked."},{"id":"journal_source_jhs_about","title":"Journal of the History of Sexuality: publisher remit","url":"https://jhistsex.org/about","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"publisher_scope_read","note":"Official journal about-page indexed extract: established in 1990; cross-cultural research on sexuality. The journal is broader than queer theory. Full-page retrieval timed out."},{"id":"journal_source_mit_jinh","title":"Journal of Interdisciplinary History: publisher remit","url":"https://direct.mit.edu/jinh","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"publisher_scope_read","note":"Publisher describes historical research using other disciplines across periods and regions. Specific quantitative and demographic programme links proposed in opusreview.md still need evidence; interdisciplinary is not a synonym for quantitative."},{"id":"journal_source_jstor_jnh","title":"Journal of Negro History: publisher remit","url":"https://www.jstor.org/journal/jnegrohistory","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"bibliographic_record_read","note":"JSTOR title-history record identifies the 1916–2001 title run and successor Journal of African American History from 2002. The end refers to this title, not the end of the continuing journal or Black history."},{"id":"journal_source_chicago_isis","title":"Isis: publisher remit","url":"https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/journals/isis/about","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"publisher_scope_read","note":"Publisher remit includes history of science, medicine and technology; inception given as 1912. Venue relationships do not indicate that these fields lack disagreement."},{"id":"journal_source_nlr_about","title":"New Left Review: publisher remit","url":"https://newleftreview.org/pages/about","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"publisher_scope_read","note":"Journal self-description includes history, social theory, politics and culture; launch in 1960. Its British origins do not make it identical to the atlas US New Left entry."},{"id":"journal_source_chicago_signs","title":"Signs: Journal of Women in Culture and Society: publisher remit","url":"https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/journals/signs/about","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"publisher_scope_read","note":"Publisher describes interdisciplinary feminist scholarship on gender, race, culture and sexuality. Specific historical programme or debate links remain to be checked."},{"id":"journal_source_jsh_mission","title":"Jack R. Censer, On a Mission: Peter Stearns and the Journal of Social History","url":"https://academic.oup.com/jsh/article-abstract/51/3/444/3980030","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"supporting_abstract_read","note":"Publisher abstract read: founding in 1967 and Stearns’s programme for establishing social history’s disciplinary position. Article published online 2017, assigned to the Spring 2018 issue; full text not read."},{"id":"journal_source_hwj_history","title":"History Workshop: Our History, 1976 journal foundation","url":"https://www.historyworkshop.org.uk/about-us/","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"institutional_history_read","note":"Institutional account identifies the 1976 founding by movement activists and reproduces the 1975 manifesto’s democratic-history purpose; later feminist subtitle distinguished from original wording."},{"id":"journal_source_annales_manifesto","title":"Marc Bloch and Lucien Febvre, À nos lecteurs, Annales d’histoire économique et sociale 1 (1929), 1–2","url":"https://www.persee.fr/doc/ahess_0003-441x_1929_num_1_1_1031","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"supporting_page_read","note":"First-page text and bibliography read. Founders introduce the new economic and social history journal and diagnose divisions between historians and researchers of contemporary societies and economies. Only the displayed first page was consulted."},{"id":"journal_source_stone_narrative","title":"Lawrence Stone, The Revival of Narrative: Reflections on a New Old History, Past & Present 85 (1979), 3–24","url":"https://academic.oup.com/past/article/85/1/3/1451461","checked_on":"2026-09-13","verification":"article_metadata_read","note":"Publisher record verifies author, title, venue, date and pages. DOI 10.1093/past/85.1.3. Full text not read in this journal pass."},{"id":"journal_source_hobsbawm_narrative","title":"E. J. Hobsbawm, The Revival of Narrative: Some Comments, Past & Present 86 (