":"Author abstract only; this is a historiographical framing, not new clinical evidence or a universal model of Indigenous experience.","checked_on":"2026-09-18","support_assessment":"supports_bounded_attribution"}]},{"id":"claim:healthgeo05:wynter_categories","subject":"work:wynter_et_al_persistence_2025","predicate":"assesses_scope","object":"concept:healthgeo05:psychiatry","statement":"Wynter, Campbell, Chaney and Marks historicize changing explanations of mental illness while tracing the persistence of racialized assumptions.","qualification":"Version-of-record opening pp. 2–3 checked; attribution to this historical analysis, not clinical guidance or endorsement of historical racial categories.","intervention_year":2025,"attributed_to":"work:wynter_et_al_persistence_2025","basis":"editorial_interpretation","valid_time":null,"review":{"status":"accepted","reviewed_on":"2026-09-18","reviewer":"Codex editorial integration review","rationale":"Version-of-record pp. 2–3 explicitly contrasts historically situated meanings with persistence. Historical categories are attributed objects of study, never endorsed medical classifications."},"history":[{"date":"2026-09-18","action":"proposed","reason":"User-prioritized coverage and identity review"},{"date":"2026-09-18","action":"recommended_for_bounded_release","decision_record":"data/extension-2026/release-candidate-06/review-decisions.json"},{"date":"2026-09-18","action":"accepted_into_production","revision":"1.122","decision_record":"data/production-batches/extension-1.122/acceptance.json"}],"evidence":[{"source_record_id":"source:healthgeo05:wynter_et_al_persistence_2025","locator":"Version of record, article pp. 2–3 (PDF pp. 3–4), lines 88–135","check_status":"passage_checked","scope":"passage","support":"Wynter, Campbell, Chaney and Marks historicize changing explanations of mental illness while tracing the persistence of racialized assumptions.","limitation":"Version-of-record opening pp. 2–3 checked; attribution to 