ification":"Selected concluding discussion, not endorsement of every earlier genealogy in the chapter. He describes an experimental programme and project design, not an inevitable transformation of the profession.","intervention_year":2004,"valid_time":null,"review":{"status":"accepted","reviewed_on":"2026-09-19","reviewer":"Codex editorial integration review","rationale":"Selected concluding discussion, not endorsement of every earlier genealogy in the chapter. He describes an experimental programme and project design, not an inevitable transformation of the profession."},"history":[{"date":"2026-09-19","action":"proposed","reason":"Restore substantive digital-history contributions after user review"},{"date":"2026-09-19","action":"recommended_for_bounded_release","decision_record":"data/extension-2026/digital-release-10/review-decisions.json"},{"date":"2026-09-19","action":"accepted_into_production","revision":"1.123","decision_record":"data/production-batches/extension-1.123/acceptance.json"}],"evidence":[{"source_record_id":"source:digital10:thomas_body","locator":"Chapter concluding discussion, captured lines 82–111","scope":"passage","check_status":"passage_checked","checked_on":"2026-09-19","support":"Thomas argues that digital historical scholarship can connect interpretation, narrative, evidence and spatial analysis, making paths of historical reasoning available to readers.","limitation":"Selected concluding discussion, not endorsement of every earlier genealogy in the chapter. He describes an experimental programme and project design, not an inevitable transformation of the profession.","support_assessment":"supports_bounded_attribution"}]},{"id":"claim:digital10:thomas_ayers_form","subject":"work:thomas_computing_2004","predicate":"assesses_scope","object":"work:thomas_ayers_differences_2003","attributed_to":"work:thomas_computing_2004","basis":"editorial_interpretation","statement":"Thomas describes his joint project with Ayers as a prismatic arrangemen